<title>USA: SEC clears Texas Utilities merger.</title>
<headline>SEC clears Texas Utilities merger.</headline>
<dateline>DALLAS 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Texas Utilities Co said Monday it has been notified by the Securities and Exchange Commission that the company's merger with ENSERCH Corp has been approved under the Public Utility Holding Company Act of 1935.</p>
<p>With SEC approval, the companies can now proceed to close the merger.  The closing of the merger is scheduled to take place in Dallas at 0900 CDT/1400 GMT Tuesday.</p>
<p>As defined in the merger agreement, each ENSERCH share will be exchangeable for 0.225 Texas Utilities share at close. ENSERCH currently has 70,494,540 shares outstanding.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
